# Where setup.sh gets the backend program when it is not next to it as "bootstrap".
# Set once by the publisher for each release (never by an owner): the address of a
# zip that holds the Linux x86-64 build, made with
#   cd backend && GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags="-s -w" -o bootstrap .
# and its SHA-256 (sha256sum of the zip). setup.sh refuses a file that does not
# match, so a swapped download cannot run in an owner's account.
#
# Left unset until a release is published; the environment variables of the same
# names override these.
# SHAREPI_BACKEND_URL="https://github.com/<publisher>/<repo>/releases/download/backend-vX.Y.Z/bootstrap-linux-amd64.zip"
# SHAREPI_BACKEND_SHA256="<sha256 of that zip>"
